  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Friday)\nIssued at 1128 AM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nRidging keeps the weather warm and dry through this weekend, \nthough high level cloudiness will continue to stream overhead. \nUpper level troughing, currently over S California, will gradually\ntransition into a cutoff low and move east this weekend. This \nfeature will eventually eject northeast into the C/N Plains Monday\ninto Tuesday. The vast majority of rainfall associated with this \nsystem is still expected to remain west and north of our area, but\na few light showers are plausible in Osage/Pawnee counties \nMonday-early Tuesday despite the dry low level airmass. Most \nguidance agrees that the cold front early next week will now \nremain just to our north, with less of a cool down expected \nTuesday.\n\nBy mid to late week, a shortwave will advance across the N Plains\nand send a stronger cold front towards the CWA. Model spread is \nhigher by this point, but if this front manages to make it into \nthe area then higher rain potential and cooler temperatures would \nlikely result. Until then, warm and predominantly dry conditions \nwill persist.",
